      ["LeanFM/EventLog.lean", "LeanFM/SessionTools.lean", "Server.lean", "McpServer.lean", "LeanFM/LLMGenerated/LeanFM.leanfm", "scripts/keepalive_check.py", "scripts/forward_check.py"]
      "LeanFM/EventLog.lean writes event lines: EventLog.line builds the envelope as compact JSON (ts as a decimal string of Std.Time nanoseconds, id = actor:seq from a per-process counter, prev = the process's last event id unless given, cause, from, to, label, protocol, version) and cuts the payload, marking truncated, so the whole line stays under 4096 bytes; EventLog.emit writes the object with the marker first ({\"type\":\"leanFM\", then the other fields, EventLog.withMarker) and a newline with one putStr and flush on the handle given (standard output, or standard error where standard output carries a protocol). EventLog.extract splits a log on newlines, parses each line, keeps the objects whose type is leanFM (dropping the marker) and requires id and label, refuses a line beginning with the marker that is not such an object, and returns the events, the count of other lines and the first malformed line's number; SessionTools.conform reads log through extract when it is given instead of events and refuses a malformed line naming it; ServerLogs.logArgs, applied on the IO side for session_conform after ProjectView.protocolArgs, replaces serverLog by the named log's text (tailBytes, first cut line dropped) and is refused where server_logs is not served or the log is missing. EventLog.sink, an IO.Ref holding the stream event lines go to, is set by each server's main (standard output for leanfm-server and leanfm-mcp over HTTP, standard error for leanfm-mcp over stdio) and left empty elsewhere, so tests write none; LeanFM.MCP.dispatchJson wraps the dispatch: with a sink, it emits Call (session = this call's id) before dispatching and Answer, caused by it, with payload {kind, bytes, status} after; conformLog keeps the events whose protocol field names the protocol checked, when any event names one, and reports the others as logOtherProtocolEvents; it first cuts the log to the window fromLine..fromLine+lineCount-1 (EventLog.window, by lines), and when the window starts after line 1 it leaves out every session with an event whose prev or cause names an id outside the window and checks the rest with allowIncomplete, reporting logLines, fromLine, nextLine and sessionsBeganBeforeWindow. Both servers emit Launch (ts = LEANFM_LAUNCHED_NS when set, from Shell to Server), then MainEntered and Listening from Server to Shell, of protocol ServerStart, which LeanFM.leanfm declares before LeanFMMcp with its obligation."
      ["LeanFM/SessionToolsTests.lean: a log mixing ordinary lines and event lines conforms through log, the other lines counted; a line beginning with the marker and broken JSON is refused naming line 3; a log of other JSON objects per line keeps only the marked ones; EventLog.line of a large payload stays under 4096 bytes and says truncated; two concatenated logs in reverse order conform the same; a log mixing ServerStart and McpCall events conforms to each protocol, counting the other's events; a window from line 3 of a two-session log leaves out the session that began before it and reports nextLine; the windows 1..2 and 3.. of a log together cover it", "scripts/keepalive_check.py: both servers' startup event lines conform to ServerStart with StartsQuickly met", "scripts/forward_check.py: a relay's wait is written as Stalled and Resumed on standard error"]
  , decision "session-real-events"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.real-events"]
      ["LeanFM/MCP.lean", "LeanFM/EventLog.lean", "LeanFM/SessionHost.html", "scripts/real_events_check.py"]
      "LeanFM/MCP.lean: Trace {h, actor, session, cause} is read by traceOf from params._meta (leanfm/session matching ^[0-9a-f]{16,32}(-[a-z0-9]{1,12}){0,3}$, leanfm/cause matching ^[A-Za-z0-9@._:-]{1,96}$) when the process has an event sink. dispatchJson, given a trace, emits the request event (Initialize, ListTools, ProjectView, SessionTool; cause = the trace's cause) before dispatchJsonCore and the answer event after it, caused by the request event, its label chosen by answerLabel from the method, whether project_view asked for a page (section or offset in its arguments, or a trace session with a child part), and the answer: success (no error and no isError), a refusal text naming a file that must be one of the listed files (NotListed), one over the answer bound (TooLarge or OverBound), else ViewError or ToolError. dispatchJsonCore takes the trace and passes Trace.disk around the IO reads: ProjectView.query (ReadRoot/Listing or ReadPage/Items), ProjectView.protocolArgs when the arguments name a file (ReadFile/FileText) and ServerLogs.logArgs when they name serverLog (ReadLog/LogLines); each pair is the child session SESSION-rN (N from Trace's own counter) and its second event is caused by its first. Trace events go through EventLog.emit with protocol LeanFMMcp and session = the host's session. notifications/leanfm/host-event is handled by hostEvent: hostRoles maps the eleven host labels to their sender and receiver; id must be host@ROOT:N for the root of the event's session, prev the same form, cause the cause pattern; a valid event is written with EventLog.line (actor host@ROOT, ts now, protocol LeanFMMcp) without touching the process's own counter or prev; an invalid one is dropped and counted in EventLog.droppedHostEvents; the answer is 202 either way. SessionHost.html makes a session of 16 random hex digits (crypto.getRandomValues), counts its events, and sends hostEvent notifications; its mcp() puts _meta {leanfm/session, leanfm/cause} in every request's params; at start it calls initialize and tools/list, writes Open, and causes its first request by Open; it writes Render after the first view's answer, and every request of the view, and the switch, waits on a promise resolved then (or when the first view fails); for each tools/call from the view, in the view's session ROOT-v1 (named in the request's _meta too), it writes Page or Load first, passes it as the cause, and writes Paged, Drawn or Refused after."
      ["scripts/real_events_check.py: against a leanfm-server in a scratch copy writing its log, a host session doing initialize, tools/list, Open, project_view, Render, Load, session_check on a listed protocol file, Drawn, and a session_check on a file not listed logs Initialize, Initialized, ListTools, Tools, ProjectView, ReadRoot, Listing, Shown, SessionTool, ReadFile, FileText, Checked, SessionTool, NotListed in that order, each with protocol LeanFMMcp and the session; the host events appear with actor host@ROOT, the view's in ROOT-v1 and each Disk pair in its own child session; a host event labelled ReadFile, one with an id of another session, and one with a bad cause are not written; a request without leanfm/session writes Call and Answer only; session_conform with protocolName LeanFMMcp over the log's window finds the conversation conforming up to the deliberate NotListed refusal, whose branch the protocol has"]
  , decision "session-event-source"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.event-source", "clause:selfhost.mcp.session.view"]
      ["LeanFM/SessionTools.lean", "LeanFM/Session/LogSessions.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Conform.lean", "LeanFM/SessionView.html", "LeanFM/SessionHost.html", "scripts/log_range_check.py", "scripts/session_view_smoke.js"]
      "SessionTools.simulate adds source {kind simulated, protocol, seed, sessions}; SessionTools.conformLog adds source {kind log, log, path logs/NAME.log, fromLine, lastLine, logLines, writers} when args carry serverLog (ServerLogs.logArgs keeps serverLog in the arguments) and {kind given, events} otherwise. logEvent reads the envelope's actor field into LogEvent.writer (bounded like every string). Thread names: SessionTools.eventJson names a simulated event's thread by its sending role (e.src); LogSessions.stream names it srcActor when the log names one, else Role@writer when the event has a writer, else the role. SessionView.html: render draws sourceBanner(body.source) first, a div.source with class simulated, log or given (each its own background colour from the theme, text at 1.25em bold) whose text is built from the source's fields only; the event JSON panel shows {event, source}. SessionHost.html has a fixed bar with two buttons, Actual log and Simulated (aria-pressed on the one shown); after its first view is shown it shows Actual log; each button sends the view a tool-input notification and then the answer: Actual log calls session_conform {project LeanFM, file LeanFM/LLMGenerated/LeanFM.leanfm, protocolName LeanFMMcp, serverLog serve, lastLines 2000, allowIncomplete true}, Simulated calls session_simulate {project LeanFM, file the same, protocolName LeanFMMcp, instances 10}, each as View's Load in the view session, answered Drawn or Refused, a refusal unmarking both buttons; the address is never rewritten."
      ["scripts/log_range_check.py: session_conform over serverLog answers source kind log with log serve, path logs/serve.log, fromLine, lastLine, logLines and writers; over events, source kind given with the count; session_simulate answers source kind simulated with its seed; a log whose events carry actor w and from Client has every stream thread Client@w, one thread for many sessions; a simulated stream's threads are exactly its roles", "scripts/session_view_smoke.js: a session_simulate answer draws the banner first with SIMULATED and its seed, a session_conform answer over serverLog draws REAL LOG and the line range, one over events draws EVENTS GIVEN; the banner text comes from source only", "scripts/view_switch_check.py: headless Chrome on /view shows the Actual log banner with Actual log pressed; Simulated shows the SIMULATED banner with Simulated pressed; Actual log brings the REAL LOG banner back; the address stays /view throughout; the page's own events in logs/serve.log conform to LeanFMMcp"]
  , decision "session-log-paging"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.log-paging"]
      ["LeanFM/LogIndex.lean", "LeanFM/ServerLogs.lean", "LeanFM/SessionTools.lean", "LeanFM/MCP.lean", "Server.lean", "LeanFM/SessionView.html", "LeanFM/SessionHost.html", "LeanFM/Session/Text.lean", "scripts/log_range_check.py", "Makefile"]
      "LeanFM/LogIndex.lean holds the pure parts: fnv1a (64-bit FNV-1a over bytes), Index {lines, size, marks, partial} with Index.scan, which extends an index by one chunk (each newline ends a line, every 1024th line's start offset is kept in marks, bytes after the last newline are a line still being written and are not counted), parseRange (lines=A-B, lines=A- and lines=-N; anything else, several ranges, or bytes= is refused) and resolve, which turns a range and a total into the first and last line or nothing (416). It also holds the IO: a table from path to an index with the fingerprint of the first line (up to 4096 bytes), the file size it has read to and an open handle positioned there; refresh reads the size and the first line, rebuilds when the file is smaller or the fingerprint differs, and otherwise reads only the appended bytes from the held handle; window opens the file, reads and discards up to the kept offset at or before the first line wanted (Lean has no seek), then collects lines until the count, 64 MiB, or the last complete line. Racing requests may both extend the index; each table entry is a consistent prefix of the file and the later write wins. ServerLogs.logArgs uses it for serverLog: it resolves fromLine/lineCount or lastLines, puts the window's text in log and the window's numbers in logWindow; SessionTools.conformLog, given logWindow, takes the text as already windowed and reports those numbers (logLines, fromLine, nextLine, logFingerprint). Server.lean answers GET /tools/logs with a Range header by ServerLogs.rangeAnswer: 206 with the redacted lines and Content-Range, Accept-Ranges and ETag, or 416. SessionView.html keeps the arguments of the last tool-input notification; given a session_conform answer whose arguments name serverLog, streamView gets a pager: an LRU map of at most 8 windows keyed by first line, Earlier and Later buttons, PageUp/PageDown at the log's edges, a request counter so only the latest request's answer is drawn, and a line under the stream with the window, the total, the open time and the hits, misses and mean miss time; a changed logFingerprint or a smaller logLines clears the map and says rotated or truncated. SessionTools.parseProtocol measures the arguments against maxArgumentBytes without log, events and logWindow when logWindow is present (the server read that window itself). Text.parse takes an optional main protocol name: the definitions before it are in reach, a name not defined is refused listing the defined ones; SessionTools.parseProtocol passes args.protocolName, and the schemas of the tools that take lean list it. SessionHost.html's Actual log sends the view a tool-input notification with session_conform's arguments (decision session-event-source), then the answer as the tool-result."
      ["LeanFM/LogIndexTests.lean: scanning a log in one chunk and in chunks of every size gives the same lines and marks; a trailing line without its newline is not counted until the newline comes; the marks of 3000 lines are offsets 0, of line 1025 and of line 2049; parseRange reads lines=5-9, lines=5- and lines=-3 and refuses bytes=0-1, lines=1-2,4-5, lines=9-5 and lines=; resolve gives (5, 9), (5, total), (total-2, total), cuts an end past the total, and none for a start past it; fnv1a of the empty input is the standard offset basis cbf29ce484222325", "scripts/log_range_check.py: in a scratch directory with logs/serve.log of 5000 lines, session_conform with protocolName McpCall over LeanFM.leanfm's text checks McpCall, and with protocolName Nope is refused naming the defined protocols; its tools/list gives session_conform an input schema with no required argument and with lastLines; leanfm-server answers Range: lines=10-12 with 206, those three lines and Content-Range: lines 10-12/5000, lines=-2 with the last two, lines=6000- with 416 and Content-Range: lines */5000, no Range with 200; a line carrying a Bearer token is redacted in the 206 answer; appending lines raises the total and leaves lines 10-12 unchanged; a line without its newline is not served; replacing the log changes the ETag; session_conform over serverLog serve with lastLines covering the whole log (over 64 KiB) is checked while the same text sent as log is refused for exceeding 65536 bytes; after two lines are appended, its /mcp answers session_conform with serverLog serve and lastLines 2 with fromLine 5001, logLines 5002, nextLine 5003 and the ETag's fingerprint", "scripts/session_view_smoke.js: a session_conform answer over serverLog with its tool input shows Earlier and the line range; Earlier fetches lines 4601-4800 once (a miss), Later shows the held window without a request (a hit), a ninth window drops the least recently used, an answer to a superseded request is not drawn, a changed fingerprint clears the windows and says rotated"]
  , decision "session-group"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.group"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Text.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Grammar.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Syntax.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Diagram.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Outline.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Global.lean", "LeanFM/SessionView.html"]
      "Text.Stmt.group name body is parsed from group Name { ... } (Grammar.group) and built as Global.box (Global.groupName name) body k, so every Global walk already passes through it; Global.groupOf? reads a group's name back from its box. Every Stmt walk in Text, Syntax, Sla, Generative and SessionTools that descends into loop and sessions bodies descends into group bodies too; build refuses continue inside a group and a repeated group name. Diagram draws the box as frame kind group and records a Group (name, top, foldable, from, to, oneWay) for diagramModel's groups, foldable when the drawing is not inside a parallel, join or sessions frame (a depth of concurrent frames carried in St); Outline adds a group node; Text.writeStmts writes group Name { ... }. SessionView starts group frames folded and draws a folded two-role group as one arrow."
      ["LeanFM/Session/GroupTests.lean: a protocol with and without the brackets has the same labels, projections, typestates, faithful rules, simulated events and conformance verdicts; the diagram has a frame of kind group captioned [Name] and diagramModel lists the group with from, to and oneWay and foldable true; the same group inside parallel or sessions is listed with foldable false; a three-role group has no ends; the outline has a group node with the block's lines; writeStmts round-trips the group; continue inside a group, a repeated name, and a name that is not an identifier are refused", "scripts/session_view_check.mjs or the view tests: a foldable group frame starts folded and a folded two-role group draws one arrow; a group that is not foldable stays open and has no fold control"]
  , decision "session-bits"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.bits"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Faithful.lean", "LeanFM/SessionTools.lean", "CtlBookExample.lean", "book/chapters/faithful-ctl.tex"]
      "Faithful.bitsOf groups the typestates by the message of their label (none written start), in order of first appearance, with each group's count and Faithful.bitsFor count, the least b with 2^b at least the count. SessionTools.faithful adds bits [{label, typestates, bits}] and hiddenBits to the rules answer and a sentence to its reading. CtlBookExample writes ctl-retry-bits.tex, the table for the Retry loop, from the same function."
      ["LeanFM/SessionToolsTests.lean: Retry's Ask and Busy each label 3 typestates and need 2 bits, Ok, GiveUp and start 0, hiddenBits 2; PlaceOrder has hiddenBits 0 and its reading says it has no hidden state; bitsFor gives 0, 1, 2, 2, 3 for 1, 2, 3, 4, 5"]
  , decision "session-buffers"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.buffers"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Grammar.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Text.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Syntax.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Realizable.lean", "LeanFM/SessionTools.lean", "LeanFM/MCP.lean"]
      "Grammar.protocolRole reads a role as an identifier with an optional [N]; Text.protocolDef keeps the names as roles and the sizes as buffers (a size above 64 refused at its position), Parsed carries buffers, and Syntax elaborates the role names as before. Realizable.explore builds each role's machine from its projection (Global.project, Local.machine, LeanGen.closure: edges and finality, refusing fork and serve) and searches breadth first over states of (each role's machine state, each role's inbox as a list of (sender, label)): a role's send edge to r with r's size 0 is one step when r's state has the matching receive edge and r's inbox is empty, delivering; with size n > 0 it appends to r's inbox while it holds fewer than n; a receive edge is taken when the front of the role's inbox matches it; an act is a step of its role. A state with no step is final when every role is final and every inbox empty, and a deadlock otherwise. Alongside each state it keeps the set of protocol states (Global.stateGraph) its deliveries can be at, advanced by each delivery and act; an empty set is an order the protocol does not allow. session_realizable answers verdict realizable or unrealizable, the problem (order or deadlock) with the deliveries leading to it, each role's inbox and waiting edges at a deadlock, the sizes and the guarantees, and the states explored under the states limit."
      ["LeanFM/Session/RealizableTests.lean: a request and answer, Images and PlaceOrder are realizable at size 0; two unrelated pairs A to B then C to D are unrealizable, naming Y before X; a role that needs two messages before it answers, fed one, deadlocks, naming its inbox and what it waits for; a size lets a sender run ahead and a full inbox makes it wait; sizes are read from Api[8] and 65 is refused; a role with parallel branches is refused naming it; session_check of a protocol is the same with and without sizes"]
  , decision "session-keywords"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.keywords"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Grammar.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Text.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Global.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Diagram.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Outline.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Chain.lean", "LeanFM/SessionTools.lean", "LeanFM/SessionView.html"]
      "Grammar.par reads parallel or par and Grammar.rec and Grammar.bounded read loop or rec; Text.lean's statement reader refuses the old word at its position (failAt: write parallel, not par; write loop, not rec), so the grammar can still say where. Text.writeStmts, Global.lines, the diagram's frame caption, the outline's labels and the chain's loop label write parallel and loop. SessionTools' JSON step kinds are parallel and loop (stepKinds, the reader and the writer). The session view finds frames by the keywords parallel and loop. Every .leanfm and .protocol file in the repository, the project specifications, the tutorial's protocols, the book generators and the book use them."
      ["LeanFM/Session/LeanSyntaxTests.lean: par { ... } and rec L { ... } are refused naming parallel and loop; parallel and loop read and write back", "LeanFM/SessionToolsTests.lean: a JSON protocol with par or rec steps is refused and one with parallel and loop reads"]
  , decision "session-syntax"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.syntax"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Syntax.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Global.lean"]
      "The protocol command is a Lean syntax extension in LeanFM.Session.Syntax. protocol Name (R1, ..., Rn) { statements } defines Name : R -> ... -> R -> Global R. Each statement elaborates to one Global constructor: msg (an Interaction with id, label, src, dst, cause and guard), act, choice, parallel, join, loop and var (rec and continue; continue ends its branch), sessions, and andThen for include. A label is a type, referred to as Option Label; the command declares an empty structure for a label that resolves to no constant (decision session-lean-syntax). cause, route (a string literal) and status (a numeral) fill Interaction.cause, route and status; no rule reads route or status. A where clause becomes a Guard holding its text, beside an unused let that type-checks it as a Lean proposition over the payload types of the ids it mentions, which must be message ids bound earlier or the guarded message itself; conformance runs the text with Session.Where."
      ["LeanFM/Session/SessionTests.lean: Purchase elaborates with its labels in order; the where clause keeps its text p.amount = q.price", "LeanFM/Session/LeanSyntaxTests.lean: a condition naming a missing field or an unbound id is an elaboration error"]
  , decision "session-choice"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.choice"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Global.lean"]
      "Global.decider takes the first steps of the branches that do something (Global.first): a message's sender or an event's role; empty branches are ignored. One role starting them all is the decider; several roles give 'no single role decides a choice, so it is a race: ' naming who starts what; no branch doing anything is also an error. choiceIssues reports the decider's error, or 'C's choice: two branches start with the same event' when first events repeat, and recurses into branches, parallel, join, loops and sessions. classicChoiceIssues keeps the classic sender-only rule for comparison."
      ["LeanFM/Session/SessionTests.lean: TransferWithTimer reports the race between Sender's Timeout and Receiver's Ack; Transfer, where the receiver decides, has no issues"]
  , decision "session-causes"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.causes"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Global.lean"]
      "Global.causeIssues walks every linear run (Global.runs) and reports a message whose cause names a message its sender has neither sent nor received earlier on that run."
      ["LeanFM/Session/SessionTests.lean: a Paid from the bank caused by an Order the bank never saw is reported (Paid: Bank never saw o); Purchase has no cause issues"]
  , decision "session-projection"
      ["clause:selfhost.session.projection"]
      ["LeanFM/Session/Global.lean"]
      "Global.project first looks for a service: Global.nestedSessions lists the bodies of the sessions blocks nested directly in the protocol's body and Global.withoutNested removes them; a role involved in some nested body but not in the rest is projected on each such body and served, one body as sessions { l } and several as sessions { offer } when their Local.firstReceives are present and disjoint, otherwise an error naming the role. Other roles are projected by projectFrom as before. Global.project r runs projectFrom r started: a role not involved in what follows projects to done; a message becomes send or recv or disappears; an event becomes act at its role; a choice the role decides becomes select, and any other becomes mergeBranches. mergeBranches flattens nested offers and accepts, as an offer, branches whose first receivable messages (Local.firstReceives, which looks inside parallel) are non-empty and pairwise disjoint, provided the role has not started or is present in every branch; a role that has not started may be absent from branches; otherwise branches that begin with the same received label must continue alike. Anything else fails with 'R cannot tell which branch C chose' (with 'after L' when two branches share their first label). sessions projects its body with started false. Global.issues collects choice, cause and projection failures for the listed roles."
      ["LeanFM/Session/SessionTests.lean: Purchase projects for the shop as select and for the bank as an offer with an empty branch; PurchaseWithHold reports that the bank cannot tell which branch the shop chose", "LeanFM/Session/ProjectionTests.lean: a client that has paid tells branches apart when one answers inside a parallel or after one; a declined branch that tells the client nothing is still rejected", "LeanFM/SessionToolsTests.lean: the two-factor login example checks clean over HTTP with notHttp for the text message; Sms projects to a service serving SendCode, Queued, Text while Auth keeps the nested sessions in place; written inline, Sms cannot tell which branch was chosen; a mailer serving two kinds of session gets an offer, and two kinds starting alike are reported; simulated logins with their text-message sessions conform, and a text session skipping the answer does not; the generated Sms starts each session at SmsS1; dropping the gateway answer is incompatible with the old version"]
  , decision "session-composition"
