      "Chain.Edge gains msgId and causeId, read from the message statement when the chain is built. Chain.generate keeps, per session, each message id's latest event (a loop rebinds it) and gives every generated event its msgId and the cause its edge names, looked up there; answers stays none, since a cause is not always a reply. SessionTools.hasLoop moves above generativeLayer, which, when the finite-path generator refuses a layer and the body has a loop, rate, event delay or periodic gate, writes an executionUnsupported note saying the chain runs it (session_simulate, session_dataset, session_mdp) and deadline monitoring does not; otherwise the generator's reason. deadlineReports returns null for a layer with executionUnsupported, so session_conform answers its structural verdict. Ride's comment says its search is unbounded on purpose and points to BoundedRide."
