      "Outline.defs scans the text line by line: defName? starts a definition at a line beginning protocol Name, braces counts braces outside string literals, -- comments and /- -/ comments (carried across lines) and says whether the line opened one, and the definition ends where its braces have opened and the depth is back where it started; a later definition of a name replaces the earlier. Outline.walk turns the global type into nodes under a parent: msg and act as message and event nodes (their line: the next line of the enclosing definition, from a cursor kept per definition, containing Label from or Label at with no identifier character before the label, and when there is none from the cursor, the first such line, as for a bounded loop's later passes, which repeat the first pass's text; choice, parallel, join, loop, sessions and group nodes take their keyword's line from the cursor and run to the brace that closes it (Outline.blockEnd, counting braces with Outline.braces), and each branch from its opening line to the line before the next } or { / } and { at the block's depth or to the block's end, the cursor set to the branch's first line before it is walked and past the block before what follows it), choice with Global.decider's role in its label and a branch node per branch, parallel and join with branch nodes and their continuation as siblings, loop with its rec line, var as continue, sessions with its body under it, and box as an include node carrying the included definition's lines with its steps under it, so their lines come from that definition. Outline.tree adds the root (the main protocol and its lines), the roles (each with ActorView.rows counts) and the definitions, at most maxNodes = 1500 through the add function, which counts the rest. SessionTools.examples compiles five texts in with include_str; withExample replaces example by its text as lean, refusing a name outside the list, a non-string, and example beside lean or protocol, and parseProtocol calls it first, so every tool takes example; MCP.withExampleArgument adds example (an enum of the names) to each session tool whose schema has lean. SessionTools.explore answers the tree, the definitions and the text, or with focus parses the text up to the focused definition's last line (with proto when given) and draws it with annotatedModel, refusing a name that is not defined or that does not end that text. fit drops svg, diagram, projections, calls and types in that order while over the limit. Dataset.Acc counts each session as it is added (paths, messages, sessions per message, sent and received per role, lengths, durations) and Acc.summary writes the same summary as before plus pathsNote when at least nine sessions in ten have a path of their own; walkCounts walks and counts without keeping sessions, refusing past maxEvents = 1000000 (bound is a parameter for tests); histogram counts with a table. The view's treePanels lays the visible nodes out left to right (column width the widest label at that depth, a leaf per row, a parent centred on its children), tweens positions over 280 ms unless reduced motion is asked for, draws edges as curves and nodes as rounded boxes coloured by kind with +n on a closed node, and hit-tests clicks through the pan and zoom; askInto calls a tool and draws its answer into one panel; run's error branch no longer swallows the success branch's else (a successful call was reported as returning no result); session_dataset calls wait up to 120 s; a dataset with pathsNote charts messages first and folds the path chart. explore with message checks the label is sent, builds the message type with Types.complete, its example with Message.example (Ty.example: integers as decimal strings, strings empty, one list element, nested messages four levels deep), its proto block with Types.protoBlock from the whole proto file, and its field with Types.payloadNumbers; with states it projects the role and turns Local.machine's methods into edges (an off