      "Global.reviewAll runs every check and returns the findings with the checks that could not run: when Global.stateGraph refuses (over Conform.graphMaxStates = 20000 states) the liveness check is listed as not checked with its reason, instead of the review failing; Global.review keeps its old contract on top of it. SessionTools.review answers findings, clean (every check ran, nothing found) or partial (nothing found, a check skipped), with notChecked and the skipped check in the reading. session_openapi puts a document over 20,000 characters in code once, compactly, without the structured copy, and goes through fit. fit drops, after the drawing and per-role detail, openapi when openapiYaml or code holds the same document, proto, and the echoed lean last, naming each. GoServer's session type gains route \"POST /api/<name>\" on its 14 Person-to-Server requests and status 200 on their responses (success and RequestRejected alike, as action and writeJSON answer), so its Server projects to an OpenAPI document of 14 operations (17 since GoServer starts at sign-in, joins games and signs out: POST /api/issue_session, /api/join_game, /api/sign_out); the demo's 405 for a non-POST /api/ request now carries Allow: POST, and TestSessionTypeRoutesAreServedOnlyWithPost reads every route from the generated goserver.leanfm and requires POST served and GET, PUT, DELETE and PATCH refused with 405 and Allow: POST."
