      ["LeanFM/Session/System.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Instances.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Grammar.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Text.lean", "LeanFM/Session/Syntax.lean", "LeanFM/Session/SpecCheck.lean", "LeanFM/SessionTools.lean", "LeanFM/MCP.lean"]
      "LeanFM/Session/System.lean holds only data, so a file declaring a system pays for nothing else: Shared (name, role, serial), Player (fresh or shared instance), Accept (protocolName, the protocol's roles, a player per role, the global type) and System. Grammar.lean adds instDecl (instance x : Role [serial];), acceptArg ([fresh] name), acceptDecl (accept P (args);), systemBody and systemCmd, registered with @[command_parser]; system is therefore a reserved word wherever the grammar is loaded, as protocol is, and Text.leanWords refuses it as a name. Text.systemDecl reads a block against the protocols defined before it and refuses a duplicate instance, more than 8 instances or 4 accepts, an unknown protocol, a player count other than the role count, fresh R in a position whose role is not R, fresh naming a shared instance, an undeclared instance, an instance in a position of another role, a player given twice, and a block that accepts nothing; fileDefs requires a system to follow a protocol and refuses a repeated system and a system or protocol sharing a name; Parsed.systems carries the blocks. Syntax.elabSystem resolves each accepted protocol, takes its roles from the explicit binders of the protocol command's definition, reads the block with the same Text.systemDecl and defines Name : System whose accepts are the protocols applied to their role names. Instances.systemsOf builds each accept's global type with Text.build, as Text.parse builds the main protocol. instancesOf numbers n instances of each accept s1, s2, ... (refusing 0 and more than 4 in all), fresh actors Role/s and shared ones Role/name. explore is a breadth-first search over PState (each instance's Conform.State and the holders of serial instances, sorted by name so one state has one key in a HashMap), at most 2000 states: for each instance, each step of Conform.nextOf is blocked when a serial instance it involves is held by another instance (recorded as what that instance waits for), else taken with Conform.step; the serial instances it involves are taken, and every instance this instance holds is given back once mentions finds its role nowhere in the instance's residual protocol; an edge records the instance, actors and whether it finished the instance (finished: nullable and no next step). A state with no step where not every instance is nullable is a deadlock; pathTo follows first-reached parents, so deadlocks are listed nearest first, at most maxDescribed = 4 described and the rest counted. isolationProblems is a pure function of edges: every actor of a step of instance s is one of s's actors, else it is a shared instance s was not given or another instance's actor. Graph.draft writes the logic tools' inline task: messages Label@s, a claim finished@s on the step after which s has finished, terminals where every instance is nullable. localize turns a formula about one instance into one about s (on X is after X@s, terminal is claimed finished@s, an atom s never shows is false and the reading says so); globalize turns after X into the or of every instance's X. SpecCheck.checkDraft is the checker call and path report that Global.checkFormula now also uses, so Spec.check, session_ctl and systems share one checker. run returns deadlocks, isolation and verdicts; SystemSpec.check lists every problem. checkActors gives the log rules: every actor Role/instance, a shared instance playing its own role and given to some accept, a fresh actor in a role some accept marks fresh and in one session only; SessionTools.conform adds them to the link problems when the text declares a system. SessionTools.instances (session_instances) reads the text's last system, explores 1 to 4 instances of each accept (default 2) with up to 8 perInstance and 8 properties formulas, and answers ok, deadlock, isolation or disproved with instances, shared instances, states, steps, deadlocks, isolation and property verdicts; it is registered in MCP, SessionTools.run and toolNames, and documented in the session reference."
      ["LeanFM/Session/InstanceTests.lean: Shop (Refresh locks db then the cache, Evict the cache then db, both serial) is a Lean system command whose accepts and players are as written and whose global type draws as Refresh applied to its roles; with one instance of each it deadlocks after Lock@s1, Drop@s2 with each instance waiting for the instance the other holds; with two of each the nearest 4 deadlocks are described and the rest counted, actors Client/s1..s4, Db/db, Cache/cache; AF terminal is disproved per instance with that path; OrderedShop (both paths take db first) has no deadlock and proves AF terminal and AG EF terminal per instance and AG EF terminal and EF Dropped for the system with 4 instances; ConcurrentShop (not serial) never waits; serial instances give fewer states than concurrent ones; a per-instance property names the instance where it fails and the label it never sends; isolation holds over every explored step, and a step reaching another instance's client or using an instance not given is reported; 0 instances and 6 in all are refused; the tools read the same system as the Lean command; session_instances answers deadlock with the path, and 625 = 5^4 states for four independent instances with every property proved, and disproved for a system never-formula; text without a system is refused with an example; the reading refuses an unknown protocol, a wrong player count, a fresh role in another role's position, an undeclared instance, an instance in another role's position, a duplicate instance, a system accepting nothing, a system named like a protocol, a system defined twice and a system before its protocols, and system as a label; the Lean command refuses an undeclared instance and an unknown protocol (#guard_msgs); a log of two Refresh sessions with actors conforms, and an actor without an instance, a fresh actor in two sessions, a shared instance in another role and an instance no accept was given are reported", "LeanFM/MCPTests.lean: session