      "One grammar, one reading. LeanFM/Session/Grammar.lean writes the grammar with Lean's parser combinators: protocolBody, requireBody, structureBody and file, statements as named nodes (msg, event, choice, declared with wbranch, parallel, join, rec, bounded, sessions, keyed, cont, incl, clock, obligation, accrue) whose construct words are nonReservedSymbol (a word is a construct only when followed by its shape: each keyword form starts with an atomic prefix, messages are tried last), annotations (frac, dur, delay, timeRef, timeExpr, qty, amount, timing, eventTiming, rate), and cond, a ParserFn that takes the raw text of a where condition up to the statement's ';' outside brackets and strings. stmt hides the recursive alternatives behind one parser with a trivial formatter. protocolCmd (optional doc comment, protocolBody) and requireCmd are registered with @[command_parser], so a Lean file that imports them parses session types with these parsers. Grammar.run parses text with the same parsers over Lean's built-in token table plus the grammar's tokens, in an empty environment, never elaborating; nesting deeper than 64 braces is refused before parsing. LeanFM/Session/Text.lean converts the syntax: name refuses dotted paths, empty, long and control-character names; nat refuses non-decimal and long numbers; fraction, duration, delay samples, time expressions, quantities, amounts (one, sample, trade vector), timings, rates and requirement clauses are checked as before; block, blocks and stmt check steps, branches and depth; protocolDef reads one protocol (roles distinct and bounded, a label equal to the protocol name refused) and unrolls bounded loops with Text.unroll; fileDefs reads a file (structures first, requirements after a protocol, no protocol defined twice) and readText runs both. fractionText, durationText and timeExprText read overlay and argument values with the same parsers. LeanFM/Session/Syntax.lean has no grammar of its own: elabProtocol reads the command with Text.protocolDef against the file's source, declares structure L for each label that resolves to no constant, and generates the Global R term from the statements (gen: msg with its Interaction, act, andThen choice for choice and declared choice, parallel, join, andThen loop, var, sessions, box with the included protocol applied to its roles; annotations contribute nothing); a guard's text is parsed with Where.parse, its ids must be bound on the path, and condTerm turns it into a Lean proposition (Or, And, Not, Eq, Ne, LT.lt, LE.le, GT.gt, GE.ge, the arithmetic classes, ids and fields as identifiers) type-checked by fun (x : Label) ... => decide (prop) in an unused let beside the Guard, whose only field is its text. elabRequire checks each clause with Text.requirement. Errors from the reading drop their line and column, since Lean reports the position. Text.parse refuses Lean keywords as names (leanWords); Text.header is written first by writeAll and by the JSON echo; SessionPanel writes it first in goserver.leanfm. Types.reserved adds Lean's keywords so a field name is a Lean field name."
      ["LeanFM/Session/LeanSyntaxTests.lean: #elab_leanfm parses each file's header (it must import LeanFM.Session.Syntax and only loaded modules) and elaborates every command in a namespace of its own with errors at the file's lines: the 13 examples/sessions files, examples/oauth/SessionType.leanfm, the six examples/vibecode protocols, exports/nested-splits/Nested.leanfm, the three book/generated/legal-session-inference files and GoServer's goserver.leanfm all elaborate; PlaceOrder, PingServer, BoundedRide, DepositSettlement, RentWithRepairs, Loan, UserLookup, SignIn, Lending and Trip-parallel agree with the text reading; an undeclared label is an empty structure and a declared one keeps its fields; a bounded loop's copies carry ids t and t_2, causes and conditions as the text reading writes them; the tools' error messages are the grammar's (expected ';', unterminated comment, unterminated string literal, nesting past 64 refused before parsing); a JSON protocol's echoed text and PlaceOrder and BoundedRide written back by writeAll elaborate (#elab_leanfm_text) and agree; negative: a missing field, an unbound id, a protocol named like its label, repeated roles, and conditions holding function application or a tactic are errors (#guard_msgs), nothing in them elaborated, and the text reading refuses the name clash and keyword names and reads past the header keeping the doc comment", "LeanFM/Session/SessionTests.lean: the purchase's guard keeps its text", "lake env lean on each session-type file elaborates it standalone"]
