      "LeanFM/Session/Skeleton.lean: Local.machine (LeanFM/Session/Calls.lean) gives a role's typestate as structured Method values (send, recv, act, offer with OfferAlt recv, nothing or other, fork, serve, cont, stop), the same machine Local.typestate prints, so the API text and the code cannot disagree. Skeleton.roleClasses writes a class per state: send_<label> calls Endpoint.send with the protocol id and cause id found by Skeleton.lookup (the unique (id, cause) of interactions with that sender, receiver and label in Global.interactions, else a cause parameter); receive tests Endpoint.accepts for each allowed message before consuming the state, binds the message's protocol id, and otherwise Endpoint.refuse raises ProtocolError; do_<label>, fork (Fork.join), serve (Server.session), again, stop and skip follow the other methods. State._take raises on a second use. Identifiers come from Skeleton.ident and Skeleton.snake, literals from Skeleton.lit (JSON escaping, valid in Python); a repeated method name in one state or a repeated role identifier throws. Global.pythonSkeleton projects every role and joins the runtime (Skeleton.runtime) and the classes. Skeleton.roleClassesTs writes the same methods in TypeScript (send<Label> via Skeleton.tail, do<Label>, fork returning a typed Fork with the join count, serve, again, stop, skip, branch<S>), a receive whose return type is the union of {label, msg, next} per allowed message, and a readonly literal state field per class; Global.typescriptSkeleton joins Skeleton.tsRuntime (Endpoint, State, End, Fork, Server, ProtocolError and the Message, LogEvent, Transport and Log types) and the classes."
      ["LeanFM/SessionToolsTests.lean: the Lending module equals examples/vibecode/lending/lending_protocol.py; Desk's S2 offers exactly send_lent and send_hold; Lent is sent as l caused by b; desk() starts in DeskS1; Librarian has skip; a loop returns to its first state; parallel forks into its branches then the continuation; repeated Ask/Reply with different causes take the cause as a parameter; colliding method names and an unknown language are rejected; hostile «names» with quotes and backslashes come out as identifiers and escaped literals with no injected line, and a line break inside «» is refused by the parser", "LeanFM/SessionToolsTests.lean (TypeScript): the Lending module equals examples/vibecode/lending/lending_protocol.ts; DeskS2 has sendLent and sendHold; DeskS6 has sendWaitlisted and no sendLent; each state has its literal state field; MemberS2.receive returns the label-tagged union; join 2 of forks with need 2; ambiguous causes are parameters; colliding method names are rejected; hostile names stay identifiers and escaped literals", "examples/vibecode/lending/typestate_errors.ts (npm run check, tsc --strict): sending Returned before a Return, Lent on an approved hold, a step on an un-narrowed receive, returning after Waitlisted, and assigning one state type to another each fail to compile, as each @ts-expect-error requires", "examples/vibecode/lending/test_lending.py: a send fills in the protocol's cause; a state used twice raises; receive refuses a wrong label, a wrong sender and another session's message without consuming the state; DeskS6 has no send_lent; the checked-in logs are what lending.py writes; every session ends"]
